1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,229
Fifteen billion dollars.

2
00:00:02,409 --> 00:00:05,163
That is how much Americans spent modifying

3
00:00:05,163 --> 00:00:07,196
their pickups in a single year,

4
00:00:07,196 --> 00:00:08,376
according to SEMA.

5
00:00:08,556 --> 00:00:11,668
Nearly thirteen million trucks got new parts.

6
00:00:11,848 --> 00:00:14,435
Lift kits, giant tires,

7
00:00:14,435 --> 00:00:16,573
bed covers, lights.

8
00:00:16,753 --> 00:00:19,106
Some of those upgrades make a truck

9
00:00:19,106 --> 00:00:20,921
better and even save money.

10
00:00:21,101 --> 00:00:23,994
Others quietly cost their owners thousands,

11
00:00:23,994 --> 00:00:26,080
every year, for as long as they

12
00:00:26,080 --> 00:00:27,022
own the truck.

13
00:00:27,372 --> 00:00:29,809
And there is one myth that stops

14
00:00:29,809 --> 00:00:32,779
many owners from making smart upgrades:

15
00:00:32,779 --> 00:00:35,825
the idea that any aftermarket part voids

16
00:00:35,825 --> 00:00:36,892
your warranty.

17
00:00:37,072 --> 00:00:39,440
The federal government says that is not

18
00:00:39,440 --> 00:00:40,230
how it works.

19
00:00:40,410 --> 00:00:42,547
In this video we go through bed

20
00:00:42,547 --> 00:00:44,065
covers, tires, wheels,

21
00:00:44,065 --> 00:00:45,099
lifts and more,

22
00:00:45,099 --> 00:00:47,720
and separate the mods worth your money

23
00:00:47,720 --> 00:00:49,581
from the ones that are not.

24
00:00:49,932 --> 00:00:52,336
Every number in this video comes from

25
00:00:52,336 --> 00:00:55,260
a published source listed in the description.

26
00:00:55,440 --> 00:00:57,890
Prices for parts vary widely by truck

27
00:00:57,890 --> 00:00:59,876
and brand, so we will focus on

28
00:00:59,876 --> 00:01:02,392
what the data shows and the trade-offs

29
00:01:02,392 --> 00:01:03,451
you should know.

30
00:01:03,631 --> 00:01:05,699
If we could not confirm a figure,

31
00:01:05,699 --> 00:01:06,638
we left it out.

32
00:01:06,818 --> 00:01:09,163
Let's start with how big this market

33
00:01:09,163 --> 00:01:09,814
really is.

34
00:01:10,164 --> 00:01:13,694
According to SEMA's twenty twenty-six market report,

35
00:01:13,694 --> 00:01:16,952
accessory and performance parts sales in America

36
00:01:16,952 --> 00:01:20,210
reached fifty-two point nine two billion dollars

37
00:01:20,210 --> 00:01:21,704
in twenty twenty-five.

38
00:01:21,884 --> 00:01:24,853
Pickup parts were the largest category,

39
00:01:24,853 --> 00:01:27,213
at thirty percent of all sales.

40
00:01:27,393 --> 00:01:29,848
Pickups and S U Vs together made

41
00:01:29,848 --> 00:01:32,687
up forty-three percent of the market.

42
00:01:33,037 --> 00:01:36,491
SEMA says nearly thirteen million pickups were

43
00:01:36,491 --> 00:01:39,120
accessorized in twenty twenty-five.

44
00:01:39,300 --> 00:01:42,548
Owners spent more than three billion dollars

45
00:01:42,548 --> 00:01:45,353
on suspension products like lift kits,

46
00:01:45,353 --> 00:01:48,084
and more than two billion on off-road

47
00:01:48,084 --> 00:01:50,225
tires for pickups and S U Vs.

48
00:01:50,405 --> 00:01:52,323
And here is the first twist:

49
00:01:52,323 --> 00:01:55,678
only twenty-six percent of people who accessorize

50
00:01:55,678 --> 00:01:58,486
their pickups actually use them off-road.

51
00:01:58,836 --> 00:02:01,665
So most modified trucks spend their lives

52
00:02:01,665 --> 00:02:02,493
on pavement.

53
00:02:02,673 --> 00:02:06,183
That matters, because many off-road parts make

54
00:02:06,183 --> 00:02:08,168
a truck worse on the road:

55
00:02:08,168 --> 00:02:10,457
more noise, less fuel economy,

56
00:02:10,457 --> 00:02:13,052
slower braking and a harsher ride.

57
00:02:13,232 --> 00:02:15,045
The best mod is the one that

58
00:02:15,045 --> 00:02:17,635
matches how you actually use your truck,

59
00:02:17,635 --> 00:02:19,513
not how you imagine using it.

60
00:02:19,863 --> 00:02:21,221
And the buyers are young.

61
00:02:21,401 --> 00:02:22,713
According to SEMA,

62
00:02:22,713 --> 00:02:25,847
more than half of accessory and performance

63
00:02:25,847 --> 00:02:27,961
parts buyers are under forty,

64
00:02:27,961 --> 00:02:30,584
and about one in four drivers bought

65
00:02:30,584 --> 00:02:34,447
aftermarket products to personalize their vehicles in

66
00:02:34,447 --> 00:02:35,832
twenty twenty-five.

67
00:02:36,012 --> 00:02:38,868
Truck modification is not a niche hobby.

68
00:02:39,048 --> 00:02:41,602
It is a mainstream American habit.

69
00:02:41,953 --> 00:02:43,801
Before we rank the mods,

70
00:02:43,801 --> 00:02:45,958
let's kill the biggest myth.

71
00:02:46,138 --> 00:02:49,840
Many owners believe that installing any aftermarket

72
00:02:49,840 --> 00:02:52,164
part voids the truck's warranty.

73
00:02:52,344 --> 00:02:55,248
According to the Federal Trade Commission,

74
00:02:55,248 --> 00:02:57,737
your warranty stays in effect if you

75
00:02:57,737 --> 00:03:00,087
use aftermarket or recycled parts.

76
00:03:00,438 --> 00:03:02,202
Here is how it works.

77
00:03:02,382 --> 00:03:04,680
Under the federal warranty law,

78
00:03:04,680 --> 00:03:06,236
the F T C says that a

79
00:03:06,236 --> 00:03:09,275
manufacturer or dealer must prove that an

80
00:03:09,275 --> 00:03:12,907
aftermarket part caused the damage before denying

81
00:03:12,907 --> 00:03:13,574
coverage.

82
00:03:13,754 --> 00:03:15,602
And it is illegal for a dealer

83
00:03:15,602 --> 00:03:18,188
to deny your warranty just because someone

84
00:03:18,188 --> 00:03:20,651
else did the maintenance or repair work.

85
00:03:21,001 --> 00:03:22,429
Now the twist.

86
00:03:22,609 --> 00:03:24,547
That protection has limits.

87
00:03:24,727 --> 00:03:27,570
If a defective or badly installed part

88
00:03:27,570 --> 00:03:30,413
damages something the warranty covers,

89
00:03:30,413 --> 00:03:32,732
the F T C says the manufacturer

90
00:03:32,732 --> 00:03:35,649
can deny coverage for that damaged part

91
00:03:35,649 --> 00:03:37,893
and charge you for the repair.

92
00:03:38,073 --> 00:03:40,797
So a poorly installed lift kit that

93
00:03:40,797 --> 00:03:43,365
damages the front axle may not be

94
00:03:43,365 --> 00:03:45,934
covered, even if the rest of your

95
00:03:45,934 --> 00:03:47,257
warranty is fine.

96
00:03:47,607 --> 00:03:49,373
The F T C also says to

97
00:03:49,373 --> 00:03:51,783
keep your maintenance records,

98
00:03:51,783 --> 00:03:54,995
because the warranty company can ask for

99
00:03:54,995 --> 00:03:55,397
them.

100
00:03:55,577 --> 00:03:57,954
Keep receipts for oil changes,

101
00:03:57,954 --> 00:04:00,411
tire rotations and inspections,

102
00:04:00,411 --> 00:04:03,264
and keep the receipts for every part

103
00:04:03,264 --> 00:04:04,215
you install.

104
00:04:04,395 --> 00:04:06,770
If a claim is ever questioned,

105
00:04:06,770 --> 00:04:09,224
paperwork is your best defense.

106
00:04:09,575 --> 00:04:10,875
Now the mods.

107
00:04:11,055 --> 00:04:13,383
We will start with the one most

108
00:04:13,383 --> 00:04:15,110
truck owners buy first:

109
00:04:15,110 --> 00:04:16,162
the bed cover,

110
00:04:16,162 --> 00:04:18,265
also called a tonneau cover.

111
00:04:18,445 --> 00:04:20,948
Bed covers come in soft roll-up,

112
00:04:20,948 --> 00:04:24,390
folding, hard hinged and retractable styles,

113
00:04:24,390 --> 00:04:27,519
and prices range from budget soft covers

114
00:04:27,519 --> 00:04:29,788
to expensive powered systems.

115
00:04:30,138 --> 00:04:31,821
Why is it often worth it?

116
00:04:32,001 --> 00:04:33,975
Security and weather.

117
00:04:34,155 --> 00:04:36,822
A locking hard cover keeps tools and

118
00:04:36,822 --> 00:04:39,712
luggage out of sight and protected from

119
00:04:39,712 --> 00:04:40,749
rain and snow.

120
00:04:40,929 --> 00:04:42,095
For many owners,

121
00:04:42,095 --> 00:04:44,354
that turns the bed into a giant

122
00:04:44,354 --> 00:04:46,905
trunk, and it can prevent the theft

123
00:04:46,905 --> 00:04:48,290
of expensive tools,

124
00:04:48,290 --> 00:04:50,404
which is a real risk for work

125
00:04:50,404 --> 00:04:50,914
trucks.

126
00:04:51,263 --> 00:04:52,459
And fuel economy?

127
00:04:52,639 --> 00:04:54,857
This is where you hear big claims.

128
00:04:55,037 --> 00:04:57,541
Some owners say a cover saves a

129
00:04:57,541 --> 00:04:58,510
lot of fuel,

130
00:04:58,510 --> 00:05:00,691
others say it does nothing.

131
00:05:00,871 --> 00:05:02,725
We could not find a current,

132
00:05:02,725 --> 00:05:04,578
independent number we trust,

133
00:05:04,578 --> 00:05:06,432
so we will not give you one.

134
00:05:06,612 --> 00:05:09,346
If a seller promises a specific fuel

135
00:05:09,346 --> 00:05:12,688
savings, ask for the independent test behind

136
00:05:12,688 --> 00:05:12,916
it.

137
00:05:13,266 --> 00:05:15,147
The downside is space.

138
00:05:15,327 --> 00:05:17,452
A cover can make it harder to

139
00:05:17,452 --> 00:05:20,749
haul tall items like furniture or appliances.

140
00:05:20,929 --> 00:05:22,675
Hard covers can be heavy,

141
00:05:22,675 --> 00:05:24,771
and some block part of the bed

142
00:05:24,771 --> 00:05:25,329
opening.

143
00:05:25,509 --> 00:05:27,720
If you often carry tall loads,

144
00:05:27,720 --> 00:05:30,446
a roll-up or folding cover that opens

145
00:05:30,446 --> 00:05:32,731
fully may be the better choice.

146
00:05:33,080 --> 00:05:34,803
Verdict on bed covers:

147
00:05:34,803 --> 00:05:37,466
worth it for most owners who carry

148
00:05:37,466 --> 00:05:41,068
tools, luggage or groceries and want security.

149
00:05:41,248 --> 00:05:44,606
Less useful for owners who constantly haul

150
00:05:44,606 --> 00:05:45,486
tall cargo.

151
00:05:45,666 --> 00:05:48,127
Buy one that fits your exact truck

152
00:05:48,127 --> 00:05:49,213
and bed length,

153
00:05:49,213 --> 00:05:52,036
and choose security level based on what

154
00:05:52,036 --> 00:05:52,759
you carry.

155
00:05:53,109 --> 00:05:56,697
Next: tires, the mod that affects everything.

156
00:05:56,877 --> 00:05:59,914
Tires decide how your truck brakes,

157
00:05:59,914 --> 00:06:02,863
steers, rides and how much fuel it

158
00:06:02,863 --> 00:06:03,297
uses.

159
00:06:03,477 --> 00:06:05,381
And in twenty twenty-six,

160
00:06:05,381 --> 00:06:07,285
tires got more expensive.

161
00:06:07,465 --> 00:06:09,185
According to SlashGear,

162
00:06:09,185 --> 00:06:12,252
the federal Producer Price Index for tire

163
00:06:12,252 --> 00:06:16,215
manufacturing rose again in August twenty twenty-six,

164
00:06:16,215 --> 00:06:19,805
and some manufacturers announced increases of up

165
00:06:19,805 --> 00:06:21,525
to five to ten percent.

166
00:06:21,874 --> 00:06:24,022
Why are tire prices rising?

167
00:06:24,202 --> 00:06:25,968
According to SlashGear,

168
00:06:25,968 --> 00:06:29,424
Michelin said in April twenty twenty-six that

169
00:06:29,424 --> 00:06:32,111
the conflict in the Middle East was

170
00:06:32,111 --> 00:06:35,336
raising its raw material and energy costs.

171
00:06:35,516 --> 00:06:38,793
Tires are made with oil-based materials,

172
00:06:38,793 --> 00:06:40,268
so when oil jumps,

173
00:06:40,268 --> 00:06:41,333
tires follow.

174
00:06:41,513 --> 00:06:43,808
That makes choosing the right tire more

175
00:06:43,808 --> 00:06:44,984
important than ever.

176
00:06:45,334 --> 00:06:48,181
Here is the twist about big off-road

177
00:06:48,181 --> 00:06:48,655
tires.

178
00:06:48,835 --> 00:06:50,016
They look great,

179
00:06:50,016 --> 00:06:52,820
and SEMA says owners spend billions on

180
00:06:52,820 --> 00:06:53,189
them.

181
00:06:53,369 --> 00:06:56,899
But aggressive mud-terrain tires are usually louder

182
00:06:56,899 --> 00:06:57,937
on the highway,

183
00:06:57,937 --> 00:07:00,637
heavier, and can wear faster and reduce

184
00:07:00,637 --> 00:07:03,960
fuel economy compared with all-season or highway

185
00:07:03,960 --> 00:07:04,375
tires.

186
00:07:04,555 --> 00:07:06,647
If you rarely leave the pavement,

187
00:07:06,647 --> 00:07:08,676
you pay for that look every day.

188
00:07:09,026 --> 00:07:11,385
The middle ground for many owners is

189
00:07:11,385 --> 00:07:12,695
an all-terrain tire.

190
00:07:12,875 --> 00:07:14,166
It handles gravel,

191
00:07:14,166 --> 00:07:16,531
dirt and light snow better than a

192
00:07:16,531 --> 00:07:19,471
highway tire, without the full penalty of

193
00:07:19,471 --> 00:07:20,259
a mud tire.

194
00:07:20,439 --> 00:07:22,573
For a truck that sees a mix

195
00:07:22,573 --> 00:07:24,627
of highway and back roads,

196
00:07:24,627 --> 00:07:27,788
all-terrains are often the best balance.

197
00:07:28,139 --> 00:07:31,354
And bigger tires can create hidden problems.

198
00:07:31,534 --> 00:07:34,818
Larger tires can make the speedometer read

199
00:07:34,818 --> 00:07:38,336
wrong, change shift points and affect braking

200
00:07:38,336 --> 00:07:40,056
and stability systems.

201
00:07:40,236 --> 00:07:43,718
Some owners need to recalibrate the truck's

202
00:07:43,718 --> 00:07:46,471
computer after a tire size change.

203
00:07:46,651 --> 00:07:49,256
Always check what size your truck can

204
00:07:49,256 --> 00:07:52,073
handle without rubbing or other changes.

205
00:07:52,422 --> 00:07:53,582
Verdict on tires:

206
00:07:53,582 --> 00:07:55,561
a good set of the right tires

207
00:07:55,561 --> 00:07:57,676
is one of the best upgrades you

208
00:07:57,676 --> 00:07:59,040
can make for safety.

209
00:07:59,220 --> 00:08:01,250
The wrong tires are one of the

210
00:08:01,250 --> 00:08:02,875
most expensive mistakes,

211
00:08:02,875 --> 00:08:05,040
because you pay in fuel and wear

212
00:08:05,040 --> 00:08:07,138
for tens of thousands of miles.

213
00:08:07,318 --> 00:08:09,814
Choose tires for how you really drive.

214
00:08:10,164 --> 00:08:11,500
Now wheels.

215
00:08:11,680 --> 00:08:14,948
Aftermarket wheels are among the most popular

216
00:08:14,948 --> 00:08:17,200
pickup mods, according to SEMA,

217
00:08:17,200 --> 00:08:19,888
along with body parts and suspension.

218
00:08:20,068 --> 00:08:22,188
Wheels are mostly about style,

219
00:08:22,188 --> 00:08:24,732
but they can also change the truck's

220
00:08:24,732 --> 00:08:26,569
weight, ride and handling.

221
00:08:26,919 --> 00:08:29,402
The twist is that larger wheels with

222
00:08:29,402 --> 00:08:32,092
thinner tires can make the ride harsher

223
00:08:32,092 --> 00:08:34,092
and the tires more expensive,

224
00:08:34,092 --> 00:08:36,506
and they may be more easily damaged

225
00:08:36,506 --> 00:08:37,334
by potholes.

226
00:08:37,514 --> 00:08:40,688
Wheels that push far outside the fenders

227
00:08:40,688 --> 00:08:42,593
can throw mud and rocks,

228
00:08:42,593 --> 00:08:45,530
and some states have rules about tire

229
00:08:45,530 --> 00:08:46,244
coverage.

230
00:08:46,424 --> 00:08:48,712
Check your state's rules before you buy.

231
00:08:49,061 --> 00:08:50,474
Next, lift kits,

232
00:08:50,474 --> 00:08:52,417
the most dramatic mod.

233
00:08:52,597 --> 00:08:54,044
According to SEMA,

234
00:08:54,044 --> 00:08:57,583
owners spent more than three billion dollars

235
00:08:57,583 --> 00:09:00,800
on suspension products like lift kits in

236
00:09:00,800 --> 00:09:04,339
twenty twenty-five, mostly for pickups and S

237
00:09:04,339 --> 00:09:04,741
U Vs.

238
00:09:04,921 --> 00:09:07,277
A lift raises the truck for bigger

239
00:09:07,277 --> 00:09:09,495
tires and more ground clearance.

240
00:09:09,845 --> 00:09:11,541
Here is the big twist.

241
00:09:11,721 --> 00:09:13,798
A lift can make a truck worse

242
00:09:13,798 --> 00:09:16,376
for most of what owners actually do.

243
00:09:16,556 --> 00:09:19,099
A higher truck catches more wind,

244
00:09:19,099 --> 00:09:20,871
usually uses more fuel,

245
00:09:20,871 --> 00:09:23,491
has a higher center of gravity and

246
00:09:23,491 --> 00:09:25,726
can be harder to load and tow

247
00:09:25,726 --> 00:09:26,111
with.

248
00:09:26,291 --> 00:09:28,876
A lifted truck can also be harder

249
00:09:28,876 --> 00:09:32,166
to park in garages and parking structures.

250
00:09:32,516 --> 00:09:35,186
And lifts can raise insurance costs.

251
00:09:35,366 --> 00:09:37,079
According to Insurify,

252
00:09:37,079 --> 00:09:39,804
trucks can cost more to insure when

253
00:09:39,804 --> 00:09:41,983
they are lifted or modified.

254
00:09:42,163 --> 00:09:45,240
Always tell your insurer about modifications.

255
00:09:45,420 --> 00:09:46,350
If you do not,

256
00:09:46,350 --> 00:09:48,410
a claim could be denied or your

257
00:09:48,410 --> 00:09:51,333
aftermarket parts might not be covered after

258
00:09:51,333 --> 00:09:52,131
an accident.

259
00:09:52,480 --> 00:09:53,891
Verdict on lift kits:

260
00:09:53,891 --> 00:09:56,174
worth it if you really go off-road

261
00:09:56,174 --> 00:09:57,450
and need clearance.

262
00:09:57,630 --> 00:09:59,490
For most highway trucks,

263
00:09:59,490 --> 00:10:01,118
a small leveling kit,

264
00:10:01,118 --> 00:10:03,832
which raises the front to match the

265
00:10:03,832 --> 00:10:06,467
rear, can give the look with fewer

266
00:10:06,467 --> 00:10:07,243
downsides.

267
00:10:07,423 --> 00:10:09,820
And remember the warranty lesson:

268
00:10:09,820 --> 00:10:11,927
installation quality matters.

269
00:10:12,278 --> 00:10:14,446
Now the mods that often pay for

270
00:10:14,446 --> 00:10:15,215
themselves.

271
00:10:15,395 --> 00:10:18,146
Number one: a quality bed liner.

272
00:10:18,326 --> 00:10:21,678
A spray-in or drop-in liner protects the

273
00:10:21,678 --> 00:10:23,269
bed from scratches,

274
00:10:23,269 --> 00:10:24,526
dents and rust.

275
00:10:24,706 --> 00:10:27,419
That protection helps resale value,

276
00:10:27,419 --> 00:10:29,822
because a beat-up bed is one of

277
00:10:29,822 --> 00:10:32,613
the first things used buyers notice.

278
00:10:32,962 --> 00:10:35,308
Number two: floor liners.

279
00:10:35,488 --> 00:10:38,241
Custom floor liners trap mud,

280
00:10:38,241 --> 00:10:39,760
snow and spills.

281
00:10:39,940 --> 00:10:42,831
They are cheap compared with replacing carpet,

282
00:10:42,831 --> 00:10:45,344
and they keep the interior looking newer

283
00:10:45,344 --> 00:10:46,035
for resale.

284
00:10:46,215 --> 00:10:48,114
It is one of the simplest ways

285
00:10:48,114 --> 00:10:50,012
to protect your truck's value.

286
00:10:50,361 --> 00:10:53,074
Number three: a proper towing setup,

287
00:10:53,074 --> 00:10:53,903
if you tow.

288
00:10:54,083 --> 00:10:55,083
A correct hitch,

289
00:10:55,083 --> 00:10:57,582
a brake controller and the right mirrors

290
00:10:57,582 --> 00:10:59,145
are not just accessories,

291
00:10:59,145 --> 00:11:00,770
they are safety equipment.

292
00:11:00,950 --> 00:11:03,074
A good setup protects your truck,

293
00:11:03,074 --> 00:11:05,455
your trailer and everyone around you.

294
00:11:05,804 --> 00:11:07,696
Number four: lighting,

295
00:11:07,696 --> 00:11:08,986
done carefully.

296
00:11:09,166 --> 00:11:12,121
Better headlights can improve safety on dark

297
00:11:12,121 --> 00:11:12,927
rural roads.

298
00:11:13,107 --> 00:11:15,780
But aftermarket lights that are too bright

299
00:11:15,780 --> 00:11:18,198
or aimed wrong can blind other drivers

300
00:11:18,198 --> 00:11:19,980
and may not be street legal.

301
00:11:20,160 --> 00:11:22,499
Choose parts made for road use and

302
00:11:22,499 --> 00:11:23,806
aim them correctly.

303
00:11:24,156 --> 00:11:26,214
Now the mods that rarely pay you

304
00:11:26,214 --> 00:11:26,536
back.

305
00:11:26,716 --> 00:11:30,340
Performance tunes and engine modifications can add

306
00:11:30,340 --> 00:11:33,312
power, but they can also affect emissions

307
00:11:33,312 --> 00:11:36,573
compliance and warranty coverage on the parts

308
00:11:36,573 --> 00:11:37,443
they change.

309
00:11:37,623 --> 00:11:39,291
Under the F T C rules,

310
00:11:39,291 --> 00:11:41,489
if a tune damages the engine,

311
00:11:41,489 --> 00:11:44,369
the manufacturer may deny that repair.

312
00:11:44,719 --> 00:11:47,017
And emissions are a legal minefield.

313
00:11:47,197 --> 00:11:49,098
In January twenty twenty-six,

314
00:11:49,098 --> 00:11:51,654
the Justice Department said it would no

315
00:11:51,654 --> 00:11:54,932
longer bring criminal charges for diesel emissions

316
00:11:54,932 --> 00:11:57,553
deletes, according to Fleet Maintenance.

317
00:11:57,733 --> 00:11:59,465
But here is the twist:

318
00:11:59,465 --> 00:12:02,378
tampering is still a violation of the

319
00:12:02,378 --> 00:12:03,480
Clean Air Act.

320
00:12:03,660 --> 00:12:07,415
The Justice Department said civil enforcement with

321
00:12:07,415 --> 00:12:09,518
the E P A will continue when

322
00:12:09,518 --> 00:12:13,873
appropriate, with penalties listed at forty-five thousand,

323
00:12:13,873 --> 00:12:17,778
two hundred sixty-eight dollars per tampered engine.

324
00:12:18,127 --> 00:12:20,782
And states can have their own inspection

325
00:12:20,782 --> 00:12:22,110
and emissions rules.

326
00:12:22,290 --> 00:12:25,145
A deleted truck may fail inspection,

327
00:12:25,145 --> 00:12:28,397
be impossible to register in some places,

328
00:12:28,397 --> 00:12:30,539
and be very hard to sell to

329
00:12:30,539 --> 00:12:31,253
a dealer.

330
00:12:31,433 --> 00:12:33,631
No jail time does not mean no

331
00:12:33,631 --> 00:12:34,010
risk.

332
00:12:34,190 --> 00:12:35,937
It is one of the worst mods

333
00:12:35,937 --> 00:12:38,073
you can make for resale and peace

334
00:12:38,073 --> 00:12:38,590
of mind.

335
00:12:38,940 --> 00:12:41,839
Another mod that rarely pays back is

336
00:12:41,839 --> 00:12:43,852
extreme cosmetic changes.

337
00:12:44,032 --> 00:12:47,360
Loud exhaust, unusual paint or wraps and

338
00:12:47,360 --> 00:12:50,856
extreme stances may make the truck unique,

339
00:12:50,856 --> 00:12:53,435
but they can shrink the pool of

340
00:12:53,435 --> 00:12:54,434
used buyers.

341
00:12:54,614 --> 00:12:55,632
When you sell,

342
00:12:55,632 --> 00:12:57,814
a truck that is close to stock

343
00:12:57,814 --> 00:13:00,140
often sells faster and for more.

344
00:13:00,491 --> 00:13:02,302
Here is the resale twist.

345
00:13:02,482 --> 00:13:04,716
Most mods do not return their full

346
00:13:04,716 --> 00:13:05,965
cost when you sell.

347
00:13:06,145 --> 00:13:08,877
Buyers rarely pay extra for someone else's

348
00:13:08,877 --> 00:13:09,268
taste.

349
00:13:09,448 --> 00:13:12,130
The parts that hold value tend to

350
00:13:12,130 --> 00:13:13,918
be the practical ones:

351
00:13:13,918 --> 00:13:15,462
bed covers, liners,

352
00:13:15,462 --> 00:13:17,900
towing gear and quality tires.

353
00:13:18,080 --> 00:13:20,392
Keep the original parts if you can,

354
00:13:20,392 --> 00:13:22,374
so you can return the truck to

355
00:13:22,374 --> 00:13:22,770
stock.

356
00:13:23,121 --> 00:13:25,350
Let's put the cost in perspective.

357
00:13:25,530 --> 00:13:26,902
According to AAA,

358
00:13:26,902 --> 00:13:30,210
a new half-ton pickup already costs about

359
00:13:30,210 --> 00:13:34,326
sixteen thousand, four hundred forty-nine dollars a

360
00:13:34,326 --> 00:13:36,989
year to own in twenty twenty-six.

361
00:13:37,169 --> 00:13:39,226
Mods are added on top of that

362
00:13:39,226 --> 00:13:39,723
number.

363
00:13:39,903 --> 00:13:42,673
A two thousand dollar lift with expensive

364
00:13:42,673 --> 00:13:45,037
tires that cut fuel economy can add

365
00:13:45,037 --> 00:13:47,064
to the yearly bill for as long

366
00:13:47,064 --> 00:13:48,483
as you own the truck.

367
00:13:48,833 --> 00:13:51,157
And fuel makes it worse in twenty

368
00:13:51,157 --> 00:13:51,932
twenty-six.

369
00:13:52,112 --> 00:13:54,878
According to the U S Energy Information

370
00:13:54,878 --> 00:13:58,991
Administration, regular gasoline averaged four dollars and

371
00:13:58,991 --> 00:14:01,970
twenty-eight cents a gallon and diesel six

372
00:14:01,970 --> 00:14:04,949
dollars and twenty-eight cents in the week

373
00:14:04,949 --> 00:14:06,509
of October nineteenth.

374
00:14:06,689 --> 00:14:09,663
Any mod that reduces fuel economy costs

375
00:14:09,663 --> 00:14:12,180
more when fuel is this expensive.

376
00:14:12,531 --> 00:14:14,795
So do the math before you buy.

377
00:14:14,975 --> 00:14:17,490
Estimate how much fuel a mod might

378
00:14:17,490 --> 00:14:20,227
cost you, add any insurance increase,

379
00:14:20,227 --> 00:14:21,929
and think about resale.

380
00:14:22,109 --> 00:14:24,672
A mod that costs one thousand dollars

381
00:14:24,672 --> 00:14:27,651
to install might cost several thousand over

382
00:14:27,651 --> 00:14:28,413
five years.

383
00:14:28,593 --> 00:14:30,793
A mod that protects the truck might

384
00:14:30,793 --> 00:14:32,239
pay you back at resale.

385
00:14:32,589 --> 00:14:35,015
Financing mods is another trap.

386
00:14:35,195 --> 00:14:37,785
Some dealers add accessories to a new

387
00:14:37,785 --> 00:14:40,164
truck and roll them into the loan.

388
00:14:40,344 --> 00:14:43,253
With average new loans at seven percent

389
00:14:43,253 --> 00:14:45,564
interest, according to Edmunds,

390
00:14:45,564 --> 00:14:48,175
you pay interest on those parts for

391
00:14:48,175 --> 00:14:48,622
years.

392
00:14:48,802 --> 00:14:53,108
Many accessories cost less from independent sellers,

393
00:14:53,108 --> 00:14:55,095
installed after you buy.

394
00:14:55,445 --> 00:14:58,060
And watch for dealer-installed add-ons you did

395
00:14:58,060 --> 00:14:58,742
not ask for.

396
00:14:58,922 --> 00:15:01,636
Some trucks arrive on the lot with

397
00:15:01,636 --> 00:15:03,152
extras like wheels,

398
00:15:03,152 --> 00:15:06,824
lift kits or protection packages already added

399
00:15:06,824 --> 00:15:07,861
to the price.

400
00:15:08,041 --> 00:15:10,499
You can negotiate those prices or look

401
00:15:10,499 --> 00:15:12,117
for a truck without them.

402
00:15:12,467 --> 00:15:14,816
Now the installation question:

403
00:15:14,816 --> 00:15:17,087
do it yourself or pay a shop?

404
00:15:17,267 --> 00:15:20,396
Simple mods like floor liners and many

405
00:15:20,396 --> 00:15:23,113
bed covers are easy to install at

406
00:15:23,113 --> 00:15:23,525
home.

407
00:15:23,705 --> 00:15:27,211
Suspension, lighting wiring and engine work are

408
00:15:27,211 --> 00:15:29,374
better left to professionals,

409
00:15:29,374 --> 00:15:31,910
because a bad install can cost you

410
00:15:31,910 --> 00:15:34,073
warranty coverage and safety.

411
00:15:34,423 --> 00:15:35,693
If you use a shop,

412
00:15:35,693 --> 00:15:38,517
choose one with experience on your truck

413
00:15:38,517 --> 00:15:41,129
model, ask for a written estimate and

414
00:15:41,129 --> 00:15:42,329
keep the invoice.

415
00:15:42,509 --> 00:15:45,725
That invoice is proof of professional installation

416
00:15:45,725 --> 00:15:48,105
if a warranty question ever comes up.

417
00:15:48,285 --> 00:15:50,171
Remember the F T C rule:

418
00:15:50,171 --> 00:15:53,551
the manufacturer must prove the part caused

419
00:15:53,551 --> 00:15:54,415
the damage.

420
00:15:54,765 --> 00:15:56,947
Here is one last twist.

421
00:15:57,127 --> 00:16:00,682
Some manufacturers sell their own accessories and

422
00:16:00,682 --> 00:16:03,148
performance parts through dealers,

423
00:16:03,148 --> 00:16:06,195
sometimes with warranty coverage included.

424
00:16:06,375 --> 00:16:07,606
They can cost more,

425
00:16:07,606 --> 00:16:09,744
but they may be the safest choice

426
00:16:09,744 --> 00:16:12,400
for owners worried about warranty claims.

427
00:16:12,580 --> 00:16:14,856
Compare both options before you buy.

428
00:16:15,206 --> 00:16:17,275
Now let's look at mods by type

429
00:16:17,275 --> 00:16:19,826
of owner, starting with the commuter.

430
00:16:20,006 --> 00:16:22,891
If your truck mostly drives to work

431
00:16:22,891 --> 00:16:25,612
and back, the best mods are about

432
00:16:25,612 --> 00:16:27,508
comfort and protection:

433
00:16:27,508 --> 00:16:29,651
floor liners, a bed cover,

434
00:16:29,651 --> 00:16:32,948
quality highway tires and maybe a better

435
00:16:32,948 --> 00:16:34,020
sound system.

436
00:16:34,200 --> 00:16:36,684
Skip the lift and the mud tires.

437
00:16:36,864 --> 00:16:38,913
They will cost you every single day

438
00:16:38,913 --> 00:16:39,616
at the pump.

439
00:16:39,966 --> 00:16:41,777
Next, the weekend camper.

440
00:16:41,957 --> 00:16:43,928
If you camp or haul gear,

441
00:16:43,928 --> 00:16:46,292
a bed cover or a camper shell,

442
00:16:46,292 --> 00:16:49,524
a bed organizer and all-terrain tires can

443
00:16:49,524 --> 00:16:51,338
make a real difference.

444
00:16:51,518 --> 00:16:53,757
A modest lift may help on rough

445
00:16:53,757 --> 00:16:56,792
forest roads, but think twice before going

446
00:16:56,792 --> 00:16:58,309
big, because a heavy,

447
00:16:58,309 --> 00:17:00,838
lifted truck can be harder to drive

448
00:17:00,838 --> 00:17:03,077
on the long highway trip to get

449
00:17:03,077 --> 00:17:03,511
there.

450
00:17:03,861 --> 00:17:04,917
Then the tower.

451
00:17:05,097 --> 00:17:06,568
If you pull a trailer,

452
00:17:06,568 --> 00:17:08,708
every mod should support towing.

453
00:17:08,888 --> 00:17:10,746
That means the right hitch,

454
00:17:10,746 --> 00:17:12,054
a brake controller,

455
00:17:12,054 --> 00:17:14,877
towing mirrors and tires with the correct

456
00:17:14,877 --> 00:17:15,703
load rating.

457
00:17:15,883 --> 00:17:18,765
A lift and oversized tires can reduce

458
00:17:18,765 --> 00:17:21,103
your truck's towing stability,

459
00:17:21,103 --> 00:17:24,063
so towers usually keep the truck close

460
00:17:24,063 --> 00:17:24,764
to stock.

461
00:17:25,115 --> 00:17:26,438
And the contractor.

462
00:17:26,618 --> 00:17:27,922
For work trucks,

463
00:17:27,922 --> 00:17:31,183
the best mods are about organization and

464
00:17:31,183 --> 00:17:33,954
security: toolboxes, ladder racks,

465
00:17:33,954 --> 00:17:37,214
locking bed covers and good lighting for

466
00:17:37,214 --> 00:17:38,437
early mornings.

467
00:17:38,617 --> 00:17:41,686
These upgrades can save time every day,

468
00:17:41,686 --> 00:17:44,283
and time is money for a business.

469
00:17:44,463 --> 00:17:47,319
A work truck rarely needs a lift.

470
00:17:47,669 --> 00:17:49,875
Finally, the true off-roader.

471
00:17:50,055 --> 00:17:52,216
If you really go off-road,

472
00:17:52,216 --> 00:17:54,211
then lifts, skid plates,

473
00:17:54,211 --> 00:17:57,868
off-road tires and recovery gear make sense.

474
00:17:58,048 --> 00:17:59,035
But even here,

475
00:17:59,035 --> 00:18:01,786
the smartest builds start small and add

476
00:18:01,786 --> 00:18:04,255
parts as you learn what your trails

477
00:18:04,255 --> 00:18:04,608
need.

478
00:18:04,788 --> 00:18:07,670
SEMA's data shows only about a quarter

479
00:18:07,670 --> 00:18:11,084
of pickup accessorizers actually go off-road,

480
00:18:11,084 --> 00:18:13,057
so if you are one of them,

481
00:18:13,057 --> 00:18:14,726
build for real trails,

482
00:18:14,726 --> 00:18:15,864
not for photos.

483
00:18:16,214 --> 00:18:18,849
Here is a twist about safety equipment.

484
00:18:19,029 --> 00:18:21,065
Modern trucks have cameras,

485
00:18:21,065 --> 00:18:24,382
radar and sensors for systems like automatic

486
00:18:24,382 --> 00:18:25,740
emergency braking.

487
00:18:25,920 --> 00:18:27,807
Some mods, like a lift,

488
00:18:27,807 --> 00:18:30,022
a new bumper or a light bar

489
00:18:30,022 --> 00:18:31,499
in the wrong spot,

490
00:18:31,499 --> 00:18:34,453
can block or misalign these sensors.

491
00:18:34,633 --> 00:18:36,824
After any change to the front of

492
00:18:36,824 --> 00:18:39,631
the truck, make sure safety systems still

493
00:18:39,631 --> 00:18:41,274
work and are calibrated.

494
00:18:41,624 --> 00:18:42,912
And check your payload.

495
00:18:43,092 --> 00:18:45,516
Every accessory adds weight:

496
00:18:45,516 --> 00:18:46,814
a steel bumper,

497
00:18:46,814 --> 00:18:48,458
a winch, a toolbox,

498
00:18:48,458 --> 00:18:49,756
a camper shell.

499
00:18:49,936 --> 00:18:52,085
That weight reduces how much you can

500
00:18:52,085 --> 00:18:52,920
carry and tow.

501
00:18:53,100 --> 00:18:55,602
Your truck's payload is printed on a

502
00:18:55,602 --> 00:18:57,965
sticker in the driver's door jamb.

503
00:18:58,145 --> 00:18:59,791
Add up what your mods weigh before

504
00:18:59,791 --> 00:19:00,711
you load the truck.

505
00:19:01,061 --> 00:19:03,522
Theft is the last consideration.

506
00:19:03,702 --> 00:19:06,021
Expensive wheels, tailgates,

507
00:19:06,021 --> 00:19:09,418
catalytic converters and tools in the bed

508
00:19:09,418 --> 00:19:11,074
can attract thieves.

509
00:19:11,254 --> 00:19:12,613
Locking lug nuts,

510
00:19:12,613 --> 00:19:15,409
a locking tailgate and a secure bed

511
00:19:15,409 --> 00:19:18,046
cover are inexpensive protection.

512
00:19:18,226 --> 00:19:21,233
And the National Insurance Crime Bureau ranked

513
00:19:21,233 --> 00:19:24,239
full-size pickups like the Silverado among the

514
00:19:24,239 --> 00:19:27,050
most stolen vehicles of twenty twenty-five.

515
00:19:27,400 --> 00:19:29,486
One more thing before you buy any

516
00:19:29,486 --> 00:19:31,445
part: check that it is made for

517
00:19:31,445 --> 00:19:32,520
your exact truck.

518
00:19:32,700 --> 00:19:34,609
Model year, cab size,

519
00:19:34,609 --> 00:19:37,700
bed length and trim can all change

520
00:19:37,700 --> 00:19:38,609
what fits.

521
00:19:38,789 --> 00:19:41,186
A cheap part that almost fits can

522
00:19:41,186 --> 00:19:43,439
cost more in installation time,

523
00:19:43,439 --> 00:19:46,127
rattles and leaks than a quality part

524
00:19:46,127 --> 00:19:48,669
that fits perfectly the first time.

525
00:19:49,019 --> 00:19:51,289
And read reviews from owners of the

526
00:19:51,289 --> 00:19:52,002
same truck.

527
00:19:52,182 --> 00:19:55,510
Forums and owner groups often reveal problems

528
00:19:55,510 --> 00:19:57,950
that product pages never mention,

529
00:19:57,950 --> 00:20:00,317
like a cover that leaks in heavy

530
00:20:00,317 --> 00:20:02,535
rain or a tire that wears fast

531
00:20:02,535 --> 00:20:03,792
on a heavy truck.

532
00:20:03,972 --> 00:20:06,712
Real owners are your best free research.

533
00:20:07,063 --> 00:20:08,398
Let's summarize.

534
00:20:08,578 --> 00:20:10,548
Worth it for most owners:

535
00:20:10,548 --> 00:20:12,518
a bed cover for security,

536
00:20:12,518 --> 00:20:14,804
good tires for how you drive,

537
00:20:14,804 --> 00:20:15,750
a bed liner,

538
00:20:15,750 --> 00:20:18,745
floor liners and proper towing gear if

539
00:20:18,745 --> 00:20:19,375
you tow.

540
00:20:19,555 --> 00:20:21,462
Worth it only for some:

541
00:20:21,462 --> 00:20:25,441
lifts, big off-road tires and aggressive wheels.

542
00:20:25,621 --> 00:20:27,012
Rarely worth it:

543
00:20:27,012 --> 00:20:31,532
engine tunes, emissions changes and extreme cosmetic

544
00:20:31,532 --> 00:20:32,227
changes.

545
00:20:32,578 --> 00:20:34,679
And never forget the three rules.

546
00:20:34,859 --> 00:20:37,529
Tell your insurer about modifications.

547
00:20:37,709 --> 00:20:40,612
Keep every receipt and maintenance record.

548
00:20:40,792 --> 00:20:43,044
And choose quality installation.

549
00:20:43,224 --> 00:20:46,208
Those three habits protect your warranty,

550
00:20:46,208 --> 00:20:48,901
your insurance and your resale value.

551
00:20:49,252 --> 00:20:51,167
So here is your mod checklist for

552
00:20:51,167 --> 00:20:52,328
twenty twenty-seven.

553
00:20:52,508 --> 00:20:54,972
One: buy mods for how you really

554
00:20:54,972 --> 00:20:56,049
use the truck.

555
00:20:56,229 --> 00:20:59,360
Two: know your warranty rights and keep

556
00:20:59,360 --> 00:21:00,003
records.

557
00:21:00,183 --> 00:21:02,180
Three: tell your insurer.

558
00:21:02,360 --> 00:21:05,459
Four: avoid financing accessories.

559
00:21:05,639 --> 00:21:08,118
And five: keep the original parts so

560
00:21:08,118 --> 00:21:10,322
you can return to stock when you

561
00:21:10,322 --> 00:21:10,666
sell.

562
00:21:11,017 --> 00:21:12,701
We put the full mod list,

563
00:21:12,701 --> 00:21:14,588
with what to buy and what to

564
00:21:14,588 --> 00:21:17,822
skip, into the Twenty Twenty-Seven Truck Buyer's

565
00:21:17,822 --> 00:21:18,226
Guide.

566
00:21:18,406 --> 00:21:20,570
